			"notes": "Kiaclef 1.0.0 is the first release of **Kiaclef, a fork of [AltoClef](https://github.com/gaucho-matrero/altoclef)** ported to **Minecraft 26.2** (Fabric).\n\n### Install\n1. Fabric Loader 0.19.5+ for Minecraft 26.2, with Java 25+\n2. [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api) 0.154.2+26.2\n3. `kiaclef-1.0.0.jar` (below) in your `mods` folder\n4. Optional, for `@build placement`: Litematica 0.28.8 + MaLiLib 0.29.6\n\nBaritone 1.19.0 is bundled. Don't install a separate Baritone or AltoClef jar alongside it.\n\n### Highlights\n- AltoClef ported from Minecraft 1.18.2 to 26.2, with Mojang mappings and Baritone 1.19.0\n- In-game control panel (**J**): live task status, item requests and lists, presets, schematic picker, command console, Stop button\n- Litematica and schematic building that gathers and crafts materials first and resumes after interruptions\n- Fixes for container tracking, crafting loops, crafting-grid leftovers, stack top-ups, and Baritone wrongly pausing on a carried chest\n\n### Verified\n1,383 unit tests pass. In automated packaged game sessions on fresh worlds, these passed:\n- diamonds from an empty inventory on untouched terrain, followed by an item list request and a schematic build\n- item lists\n- Litematica building with mid-build recovery\n- containers\n- the kelp crafting chain\n- Mob Defense task selection\n- the control panel\n\n### Known limits\n- Weak night survival: Mob Defense reacts late to creepers and Drowned.\n- Speedrun (`@gamer`), natural Nether/End travel, real combat, multiplayer, large schematics, and most catalogue items are untested.\n\n### Credits\nAltoClef by TacoTechnica and contributors (MIT). Baritone by leijurv, Brady and contributors (LGPL-3.0, bundled unmodified). See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the repository.\n\nSHA-256 checksums are in `SHA256SUMS.txt`."
		}
